Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “CLUSTERS”: identify cluster 41 rows  
• “CELL_TYPE_COARSE”, “CELL_TYPE_FINE”, “CELL_TYPE_GENERAL”, “CELL_TYPE”: restrict to epithelial cells  
• “SEX” (and/or “SEX_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID”): split rows into female vs male  
• “DEVELOPMENT_STAGE” and/or “DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID”: locate 74‑year‑old‑human‑stage patients  
• “X_VALUE”: log‑normalized expression value used for averaging  
• “FEATURE_NAME”: gene symbol whose expression is being compared  
• (optional) “HTAN_PARTICIPANT_ID”, “DONOR_ID”, “BATCH”: check individual or batch level if needed  
• (optional) columns from CLINICAL_TIER1_DIAGNOSIS_CURRENT (e.g. “Age_at_Diagnosis”) if cross‑checking age is desired  

Typical filter conditions to isolate the cohort  
1. "CLUSTERS" = '41'  
2. "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'  (or other epithelial‑related columns)  
3. ("DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74‑year‑old%' OR "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000172')  
4. "SEX" IN ('female','male')  (or “SEX_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID” IN ('PATO:0000383','PATO:0000384'))  

