Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “CLUSTERS”: identify cluster 41 rows  
• “CELL_TYPE_COARSE”, “CELL_TYPE_FINE”, “CELL_TYPE_GENERAL”, “CELL_TYPE”: restrict to epithelial cells  
• “SEX” (and/or “SEX_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID”): split rows into female vs male  
• “DEVELOPMENT_STAGE” and/or “DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID”: locate 74‑year‑old‑human‑stage patients  
• “X_VALUE”: log‑normalized expression value used for averaging  
• “FEATURE_NAME”: gene symbol whose expression is being compared  
• (optional) “HTAN_PARTICIPANT_ID”, “DONOR_ID”, “BATCH”: check individual or batch level if needed  
• (optional) columns from CLINICAL_TIER1_DIAGNOSIS_CURRENT (e.g. “Age_at_Diagnosis”) if cross‑checking age is desired  

Typical filter conditions to isolate the cohort  
1. "CLUSTERS" = '41'  
2. "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'  (or other epithelial‑related columns)  
3. ("DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74‑year‑old%' OR "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000172')  
4. "SEX" IN ('female','male')  (or “SEX_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID” IN ('PATO:0000383','PATO:0000384'))  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspections to the final analytical step.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double‑quotes and only the two allowed tables are referenced.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List the distinct cluster labels present in the scRNA‑seq table
SELECT DISTINCT "CLUSTERS"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Peek at 20 epithelial cells that belong specifically to cluster 41
SELECT "HTAN_BIOSPECIMEN_ID",
       "CLUSTERS",
       "CELL_TYPE_COARSE",
       "CELL_TYPE",
       "SEX",
       "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE",
       "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show the various DEVELOPMENT_STAGE text strings seen in cluster 41
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CLUSTERS" = '41'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Verify how the 74‑year‑old human stage is encoded (text search)
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE",
       "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74%year%old%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Get distinct SEX values within epithelial cluster 41, 74‑year‑old stage cohort
SELECT DISTINCT "SEX", "SEX_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74%year%old%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: List 20 random gene‑expression rows for the female subset (quality check)
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       "X_VALUE",
       "SEX",
       "CLUSTERS",
       "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE" ILIKE '%74%year%old%'
  AND "SEX" ILIKE 'female'
LIMIT 20;
```

